1
00:00:19,639 --> 00:00:21,683
I've come with a request

2
00:00:21,724 --> 00:00:24,436
regarding the story
of Sherlock Holmes

3
00:00:24,478 --> 00:00:28,648
and his nemesis, Professor
William James Moriarty.

4
00:00:28,690 --> 00:00:32,068
Would you kindly
bring it to a close?

5
00:00:32,110 --> 00:00:33,903
As you wish.

6
00:00:38,367 --> 00:00:39,575
[HOLMES]
What's that?

7
00:00:39,617 --> 00:00:42,120
[WILLIAM]
The final location and time.

8
00:00:42,162 --> 00:00:44,789
Also, the address
of another place

9
00:00:44,831 --> 00:00:47,167
that will provide
further answers.

10
00:00:53,548 --> 00:00:54,883
[HOLMES]
Liam.

11
00:00:56,051 --> 00:00:59,971
Why me? Out of all the people.

12
00:01:00,013 --> 00:01:02,974
You composed the mysteries;
my role was nothing more

13
00:01:03,016 --> 00:01:05,268
than to be the detective
who'd solve them.

14
00:01:06,353 --> 00:01:08,021
[HOLMES]
So, why then?

15
00:01:08,063 --> 00:01:09,939
Why did it have to be me?

16
00:01:16,946 --> 00:01:20,325
- -[bell tolling]
- -[WILLIAM] Because--

17
00:01:24,579 --> 00:01:26,289
[WILLIAM]
Our time's up.

18
00:03:01,676 --> 00:03:04,679
[WATSON]
This is an address in the slums.

19
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:06,181
It's obvious.

20
00:03:06,222 --> 00:03:09,392
There's something here
he wants you to discover.

21
00:03:09,434 --> 00:03:11,769
You should go and
find out what it is.

22
00:03:11,811 --> 00:03:13,938
John, go there with me.

23
00:03:13,980 --> 00:03:16,774
[WATSON] No, you're the
one he delegated this to.

24
00:03:16,816 --> 00:03:18,693
Not me.

25
00:03:18,734 --> 00:03:22,989
This man, you're
going to save him, yes?

26
00:03:23,031 --> 00:03:28,411
I know you'll do whatever
you believe is right.

27
00:03:28,453 --> 00:03:29,871
[HOLMES grunts]

28
00:03:34,417 --> 00:03:35,918
[MORAN]
Hey, Albert.

29
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:38,505
There's one last thing
I wanted to ask.

30
00:03:38,547 --> 00:03:41,257
[ALBERT]
What is it, Colonel?

31
00:03:41,299 --> 00:03:45,053
[MORAN] It's just, I was
prepared to die with William

32
00:03:45,094 --> 00:03:48,640
and atone for the
crimes we've committed.

33
00:03:48,682 --> 00:03:52,185
Everyone who assembled
here felt the same.

34
00:03:53,728 --> 00:03:56,981
This new plan leaves
Will to take our sins

35
00:03:57,023 --> 00:03:59,693
with him to the grave.

36
00:03:59,734 --> 00:04:03,196
In other words,
he's telling us to live on.

37
00:04:05,114 --> 00:04:10,036
What are you planning to do
with your life... after this?

38
00:04:10,078 --> 00:04:13,164
As survivors, the only
thing we are capable of

39
00:04:13,206 --> 00:04:15,500
doing in our predicament.

40
00:04:17,085 --> 00:04:21,256
[ALBERT] I cannot bear the cross
with him, not now at least.

41
00:04:21,297 --> 00:04:23,925
But I can carry it afterwards.

42
00:04:26,052 --> 00:04:29,639
Passed down from brother
to brother. Shame.

43
00:04:48,241 --> 00:04:50,076
[WILLIAM]
Once the demon is exorcised,

44
00:04:50,118 --> 00:04:53,705
the heart can become pure,
and the curse, lifted.

45
00:04:53,747 --> 00:04:58,334
Mark my words, this
country will be purified.

46
00:04:58,376 --> 00:05:02,505
As a nobleman,
I bet you'd like that,

47
00:05:02,547 --> 00:05:06,468
to see me taken
away in shackles.

48
00:05:06,509 --> 00:05:10,472
[ALBERT] With those words,
you opened up my eyes

49
00:05:10,513 --> 00:05:14,643
and showed me a world
that could be.

50
00:05:14,684 --> 00:05:19,814
Since that day, the plan has
not been altered one stitch.

51
00:05:19,855 --> 00:05:23,276
William, my dear brother,

52
00:05:23,318 --> 00:05:27,530
you anticipated this
outcome from the beginning.

53
00:05:31,867 --> 00:05:35,079
[FRED] Fire! The Lord of Crime
is burning the city down!

54
00:05:35,121 --> 00:05:36,289
[MAN 24A]
The Lord of Crime?

55
00:05:36,331 --> 00:05:39,041
[MAN 24B] Those buildings
are empty, aren't they?

56
00:05:49,093 --> 00:05:51,971
I have been expecting you, sir.

57
00:05:54,683 --> 00:05:56,309
[HOLMES]
What's this?

58
00:05:57,393 --> 00:06:00,896
[HOLMES] Blueprints for
the Noahtic and directions,

59
00:06:00,938 --> 00:06:03,817
enabling Hope
to enter the mansion.

60
00:06:03,858 --> 00:06:07,320
A collection of criminal plans
drawn up by Master William.

61
00:06:07,362 --> 00:06:08,863
A museum, of sorts.

62
00:06:08,904 --> 00:06:12,784
But this final note,
I was told to hand deliver.

63
00:06:19,749 --> 00:06:23,419
[WILLIAM] I'm grateful that
you came this far, Sherlock.

64
00:06:23,461 --> 00:06:28,132
First off, I'd like to thank you
for humoring my request.

65
00:06:28,174 --> 00:06:31,678
As you are aware, my aim is
to assume full responsibility

66
00:06:31,720 --> 00:06:33,888
in regards to this plan.

67
00:06:33,929 --> 00:06:38,601
Slowly, but surely,
I believe my plot will succeed.

68
00:06:38,643 --> 00:06:41,937
The hearts of the people
will be swayed in time.

69
00:06:41,979 --> 00:06:45,941
Alas, I won't be able to
see the results myself,

70
00:06:45,983 --> 00:06:48,277
but that cannot be helped.

71
00:06:48,319 --> 00:06:51,573
Thus, I must
make another request.

72
00:06:52,699 --> 00:06:55,660
[WILLIAM] Amidst this great
upheaval, there will be many

73
00:06:55,702 --> 00:06:59,121
voices that cry out for
help and receive none.

74
00:06:59,163 --> 00:07:03,418
So, I would ask
that you help them.

75
00:07:10,466 --> 00:07:14,554
[WILLIAM] One more thing,
when I came to call on you...

76
00:07:15,513 --> 00:07:18,099
[WILLIAM] ...you likely
left me with a question.

77
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:21,895
Something along the
lines of, why you?

78
00:07:21,936 --> 00:07:25,607
Giving a single reason
would prove rather difficult.

79
00:07:25,648 --> 00:07:27,650
But let it suffice to say,

80
00:07:27,692 --> 00:07:29,652
our first meeting
was enjoyable enough

81
00:07:29,694 --> 00:07:33,740
for me to forget my plan,
for a moment at least.

82
00:07:34,783 --> 00:07:37,410
[WILLIAM] It felt as though
I had found the one person

83
00:07:37,452 --> 00:07:39,161
who understood me.

84
00:07:39,203 --> 00:07:41,414
Had our circumstances
been different,

85
00:07:41,456 --> 00:07:45,000
I would have liked to converse
with you at great length.

86
00:07:45,042 --> 00:07:47,712
For reasons I
can't quite explain,

87
00:07:47,754 --> 00:07:51,674
it feels as though you're
a long-standing friend.

88
00:07:51,716 --> 00:07:54,886
That is why
I want you at my side

89
00:07:54,928 --> 00:07:59,682
at the moment I meet my end;
no one else will do.

90
00:08:00,975 --> 00:08:06,773
[WILLIAM] If only we could
be reborn in another world.

91
00:08:06,815 --> 00:08:12,445
Perhaps, in the next life,
things will be different.

92
00:08:15,323 --> 00:08:18,033
If only, Liam.

93
00:08:18,075 --> 00:08:21,245
Genius couldn't tell I felt
the same way this whole time.

94
00:08:21,287 --> 00:08:23,957
[growls] The bloody fool!

95
00:08:32,632 --> 00:08:34,592
[NOBLES murmuring]

96
00:08:34,634 --> 00:08:36,344
Quite an ominous sight.

97
00:08:36,385 --> 00:08:37,679
From what I've heard,

98
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:40,640
the Lord of Crime has been
setting fires all over London.

99
00:08:40,682 --> 00:08:42,266
[TOWNSEND]
The Lord of Crime?

100
00:08:42,308 --> 00:08:43,852
[NOBLEMAN 24A]
No need to worry, though.

101
00:08:43,893 --> 00:08:46,980
Thankfully, all of the fires
are confined to the slums.

102
00:08:47,021 --> 00:08:48,731
Just the slums, eh?

103
00:08:48,773 --> 00:08:52,234
Moriarty has the nobility on
edge thinking we're his enemy,

104
00:08:52,276 --> 00:08:55,530
but it turns out the man's
bloodlust is egalitarian.

105
00:08:55,571 --> 00:08:57,448
[TOWNSEND, NOBLEMEN laugh]

106
00:08:57,490 --> 00:08:59,492
[EMPLOYEE 24A]
Lord Townsend, sir!

107
00:08:59,534 --> 00:09:02,662
[TOWNSEND, NOBLES panting]

108
00:09:02,704 --> 00:09:04,038
[TOWNSEND]
What do you mutts want?

109
00:09:04,079 --> 00:09:05,331
Please, Lord Townsend!

110
00:09:05,373 --> 00:09:07,917
The fires are out of control;
we need to use the water

111
00:09:07,959 --> 00:09:10,127
from the loading
dock to put them out!

112
00:09:10,169 --> 00:09:12,672
[TOWNSMAN 24B] The mansions
completely surround the river!

113
00:09:12,714 --> 00:09:15,008
There's no place
for us to draw it from!

114
00:09:15,049 --> 00:09:17,134
[TOWNSMAN 24C] But if you
let us pass through your gate,

115
00:09:17,176 --> 00:09:19,804
we'll have a fighting
chance of stopping the flames!

116
00:09:19,846 --> 00:09:22,097
Please, sir! We're begging you!

117
00:09:22,139 --> 00:09:23,432
[TOWNSEND]
Off with you!

118
00:09:23,474 --> 00:09:26,268
As if I would allow a rabble
to set foot on my property!

119
00:09:26,310 --> 00:09:28,062
But, sir, please.

120
00:09:28,103 --> 00:09:30,857
Away with you! If you do not
leave this very instant,

121
00:09:30,899 --> 00:09:33,275
then you can consider
yourselves unemployed

122
00:09:33,317 --> 00:09:34,276
come tomorrow morning!

123
00:09:34,318 --> 00:09:35,862
[TOWNSPEOPLE gasp]

124
00:09:41,659 --> 00:09:43,160
The flames are getting closer!

125
00:09:43,202 --> 00:09:44,871
[TOWNSMAN 24A]
We're begging you, Lord Townsend!

126
00:09:44,913 --> 00:09:48,290
Open the gate! Please!
Before it reaches us!

127
00:09:48,332 --> 00:09:52,545
At this rate, we'll all be--
The city of London will be--

128
00:09:52,587 --> 00:09:53,546
[NOBLES gasp]

129
00:09:53,588 --> 00:09:55,715
[TOWNSEND]
Stop that! What are you doing?

130
00:09:55,757 --> 00:09:57,050
[NOBLES gasp]

131
00:09:57,091 --> 00:09:58,467
You won't open up.

132
00:09:58,509 --> 00:10:01,387
So we'll have to get through
and reach the water on our own.

133
00:10:01,429 --> 00:10:03,138
Did you not hear me, man?!

134
00:10:03,180 --> 00:10:04,849
You will not overrun my estate!

135
00:10:04,891 --> 00:10:07,101
Someone, stop them!

136
00:10:07,142 --> 00:10:09,938
[MORAN] Just which side
is hard of hearing?

137
00:10:09,979 --> 00:10:11,522
London is burning,

138
00:10:11,564 --> 00:10:13,691
and these people are
asking for your help.

139
00:10:13,733 --> 00:10:17,152
If nothing is done,
everything will turn to ash,

140
00:10:17,194 --> 00:10:20,573
and this country is finished.

141
00:10:20,615 --> 00:10:26,161
"Noblesse oblige," the mandatory
obligation of the nobility.

142
00:10:26,203 --> 00:10:29,082
While we've all risked our
lives to put out the fire,

143
00:10:29,123 --> 00:10:31,500
you rich have done nothing.

144
00:10:31,542 --> 00:10:34,670
So which of us here
are the true nobility?

145
00:10:34,712 --> 00:10:36,631
[TOWNSEND grunts]
Silence!

146
00:10:36,672 --> 00:10:38,466
We are noblemen
and women by birth,

147
00:10:38,507 --> 00:10:40,009
bearing highborn blood!

148
00:10:40,051 --> 00:10:41,218
Whereas you lot are simply--

149
00:10:41,260 --> 00:10:42,929
[MORAN]
Let me ask you.

150
00:10:42,971 --> 00:10:45,848
Were your ancestors
born into the nobility?

151
00:10:47,058 --> 00:10:53,230
Of course not, they gave
everything for this country.

152
00:10:53,272 --> 00:10:54,857
Those offerings differ

153
00:10:54,899 --> 00:10:58,569
based on one's position
and what they have to sacrifice.

154
00:10:58,611 --> 00:11:03,741
How they think, how they act,
and accept responsibility.

155
00:11:03,783 --> 00:11:05,994
That's what made one a noble,

156
00:11:06,035 --> 00:11:09,246
not their birth,
or how wealthy they were,

157
00:11:09,288 --> 00:11:13,417
but their willingness to make
sacrifices for their country.

158
00:11:13,459 --> 00:11:16,587
[NOBLES murmur]

159
00:11:19,048 --> 00:11:23,427
[TOWNSPEOPLE gasp]

160
00:11:23,469 --> 00:11:24,846
[TOWNSEND]
Keep those buckets coming!

161
00:11:24,887 --> 00:11:26,806
[NOBLES]
Yes, sir!

162
00:11:46,742 --> 00:11:51,413
[TOWNSPEOPLE murmur]

163
00:11:51,455 --> 00:11:53,499
Somehow, we put it out.

164
00:11:53,541 --> 00:11:56,502
[NOBLEMAN 24B grunts]
It's a miracle.

165
00:11:58,671 --> 00:12:00,923
[MORAN] All is proceeding
as planned, William.

166
00:12:00,965 --> 00:12:03,551
Just one thing left.

167
00:12:03,592 --> 00:12:05,469
The finale.

168
00:12:15,563 --> 00:12:17,982
[TOWNSPEOPLE murmuring]

169
00:12:18,024 --> 00:12:20,317
[NOBLEMAN 24C] Wh-What was
that burst of light just now?

170
00:12:20,359 --> 00:12:22,070
[TOWNSMAN 24C]
Look! Atop the bridge!

171
00:12:24,279 --> 00:12:25,489
[TOWNSMAN 24D]
Isn't that...?

172
00:12:25,531 --> 00:12:27,449
[TOWNSMAN 24C]
It's Sherlock Holmes!

173
00:12:27,491 --> 00:12:31,620
[NOBLEMAN 24C] And the other man
is Moriarty, the Lord of Crime!

174
00:12:31,662 --> 00:12:34,289
[TOWNSMAN 24D] Holmes has
got the scoundrel cornered!

175
00:12:36,209 --> 00:12:40,755
You have arrived precisely
on time, Sherlock. No surprise.

176
00:12:40,796 --> 00:12:44,800
Years of planning,
all leading up to this moment.

177
00:12:44,842 --> 00:12:48,054
Using the fires to make the
nobility and the townsfolk

178
00:12:48,096 --> 00:12:51,390
overcome their class barrier
in defense of their city.

179
00:12:51,432 --> 00:12:54,351
[HOLMES]
And then, standing together,

180
00:12:54,393 --> 00:12:59,148
they focus their collective
rage at one target.

181
00:12:59,190 --> 00:13:02,944
All of London considers
you to be a devil, Liam.

182
00:13:04,278 --> 00:13:06,572
[HOLMES]
But there is still time.

183
00:13:06,614 --> 00:13:08,323
Come with me.

184
00:13:08,365 --> 00:13:10,367
Together, I know we
can find a solution

185
00:13:10,409 --> 00:13:12,453
that doesn't end in death!

186
00:13:16,791 --> 00:13:21,003
[WILLIAM sighs]
I'm beyond redemption,

187
00:13:21,045 --> 00:13:24,298
yet still you try to tempt
me to cling to life!

188
00:13:26,550 --> 00:13:29,595
[WILLIAM] If there is
a devil here, it's you!

189
00:13:29,637 --> 00:13:30,596
[WILLIAM yells]

190
00:13:30,638 --> 00:13:33,099
[BOTH grunting]

191
00:13:36,144 --> 00:13:39,688
[MORAN] Louis, are you
sure you want to watch this?

192
00:13:39,730 --> 00:13:42,733
[LOUIS] I requested Holmes'
services in this matter...

193
00:13:42,775 --> 00:13:45,360
...to save Brother.

194
00:13:45,402 --> 00:13:47,947
I'm only here to
see things through,

195
00:13:47,989 --> 00:13:50,491
until the curtains fall.

196
00:13:50,532 --> 00:13:55,788
I gave up my entire life for
Brother, to further his ideals.

197
00:13:55,830 --> 00:13:59,125
I did not mind knowing
death was a certainty,

198
00:13:59,167 --> 00:14:02,253
as long as we
could die together.

199
00:14:03,629 --> 00:14:08,926
[LOUIS] That was before, he
decided he needed to die alone.

200
00:14:08,968 --> 00:14:11,262
One thought terrified me,

201
00:14:11,304 --> 00:14:14,389
being left behind,
alone in this world.

202
00:14:14,431 --> 00:14:17,935
I was convinced there
would be no point in going on.

203
00:14:17,977 --> 00:14:22,815
I had absolutely nothing to
call my own, no possessions.

204
00:14:22,857 --> 00:14:24,817
Whenever I had these thoughts,

205
00:14:24,859 --> 00:14:29,238
Brother would always step in
and affirm my existence.

206
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:34,160
Reassuring me I deserved
to be a part of this world.

207
00:14:34,202 --> 00:14:36,996
No matter the conclusion
that is reached tonight,

208
00:14:37,038 --> 00:14:40,208
I know that I will
live to see tomorrow.

209
00:14:41,667 --> 00:14:43,377
[LOUIS]
The truth is,

210
00:14:43,418 --> 00:14:46,839
if any single person
acknowledged my existence,

211
00:14:46,881 --> 00:14:48,883
I could go on living.

212
00:14:49,925 --> 00:14:52,928
[LOUIS] And if Holmes
is that man for Brother,

213
00:14:52,970 --> 00:14:57,474
the same way Brother has
been for me, that's enough.

214
00:14:59,018 --> 00:15:01,145
They've all seen us now,

215
00:15:01,187 --> 00:15:03,189
witnessed the
great detective battling

216
00:15:03,231 --> 00:15:05,691
against the Lord of Crime.

217
00:15:05,733 --> 00:15:06,984
The time has come.

218
00:15:07,026 --> 00:15:10,696
Do you really expect me to
stand by and watch you die?

219
00:15:10,738 --> 00:15:14,200
A mind like yours and
that's your idea of atonement?

220
00:15:14,242 --> 00:15:18,453
It's simply a means of
avoiding your own suffering!

221
00:15:18,495 --> 00:15:21,415
Don't use death
as an escape act!

222
00:15:21,456 --> 00:15:22,958
You're not past redemption--

223
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,711
you're just taking
the easy way out!

224
00:15:25,753 --> 00:15:30,007
Live and atone for
what you've done.

225
00:15:30,049 --> 00:15:35,054
Liam, take my hand and live.

226
00:15:46,815 --> 00:15:48,525
[HOLMES gasps]

227
00:15:55,908 --> 00:15:58,160
[HOLMES]
You stubborn jackass!

228
00:16:01,205 --> 00:16:03,916
[HOLMES groans]

229
00:16:05,167 --> 00:16:09,422
You're mad. Why would
you try to save me?

230
00:16:09,463 --> 00:16:11,173
[HOLMES]
Isn't it clear?

231
00:16:11,215 --> 00:16:15,052
Because, William Moriarty,
you are my friend.

232
00:16:15,094 --> 00:16:17,596
[WILLIAM grunts]

233
00:16:17,638 --> 00:16:20,766
[HOLMES] Existence may be
a bitter venture for you,

234
00:16:20,808 --> 00:16:23,394
but not for the world
you've brought about.

235
00:16:23,436 --> 00:16:27,440
It's a place worth
living in, I'm sure of it!

236
00:16:27,481 --> 00:16:28,816
That future--

237
00:16:28,857 --> 00:16:31,485
Our future could
be yours as well!

238
00:16:31,526 --> 00:16:34,363
Experience it for yourself!

239
00:16:34,405 --> 00:16:37,783
So, climb up and live!

240
00:16:39,827 --> 00:16:42,246
[WILLIAM]
I'm a fool.

241
00:16:42,288 --> 00:16:45,082
You didn't come
here as a detective,

242
00:16:45,124 --> 00:16:49,128
but rather, as a friend.

243
00:16:49,170 --> 00:16:52,631
You've bested me, Sherly.

244
00:16:53,507 --> 00:16:55,050
[gasps]

245
00:16:55,092 --> 00:16:56,844
[yells]

246
00:17:03,476 --> 00:17:07,229
You idiot, as if
that would stop me!

247
00:17:26,623 --> 00:17:30,627
Sorry, you can't.

248
00:17:30,669 --> 00:17:35,090
Both of us, we have to live.

249
00:17:51,482 --> 00:17:54,068
[LOUIS]
Three months have now passed.

250
00:17:54,109 --> 00:17:55,777
Albert has
relinquished his fortune

251
00:17:55,819 --> 00:17:57,905
to begin a recovery effort,

252
00:17:57,946 --> 00:18:00,908
the family name
was kept out of it.

253
00:18:00,949 --> 00:18:03,452
Additionally, several
other aristocrats

254
00:18:03,494 --> 00:18:06,830
have contributed
to the fund as well.

255
00:18:06,872 --> 00:18:10,834
Despite a large-scale search
effort undertaken by the Yard,

256
00:18:10,876 --> 00:18:14,171
William's body was never
recovered from the river.

257
00:18:16,006 --> 00:18:19,552
[LOUIS]
However, I'm sure...

258
00:18:19,593 --> 00:18:22,221
[MYCROFT]
Ah, so you showed up.

259
00:18:22,263 --> 00:18:25,391
[LOUIS grunts]
Is this...?

260
00:18:25,433 --> 00:18:26,767
[MYCROFT]
Yes.

261
00:18:26,808 --> 00:18:30,438
It's a collection of all the
incidents put into story form.

262
00:18:30,479 --> 00:18:32,523
Soon it will be going on sale,

263
00:18:32,565 --> 00:18:35,984
but I received a copy
from the author, Doctor Watson.

264
00:18:38,279 --> 00:18:41,907
There is no cause to worry.
I have read it.

265
00:18:41,949 --> 00:18:43,451
Concerning the villain,

266
00:18:43,492 --> 00:18:46,537
Professor Moriarty
is evil personified.

267
00:18:48,205 --> 00:18:49,582
How curious.

268
00:18:49,623 --> 00:18:50,749
Seems he penned the work

269
00:18:50,791 --> 00:18:53,586
with full knowledge of
what actually transpired.

270
00:18:57,756 --> 00:18:59,925
On behalf of Great Britain,

271
00:18:59,967 --> 00:19:02,803
I offer my heartfelt
gratitude to you

272
00:19:02,844 --> 00:19:05,680
and your three brothers.

273
00:19:05,722 --> 00:19:08,225
Sherlock pushed a
secret arrangement,

274
00:19:08,267 --> 00:19:09,977
one that would abolish
the House of Lords

275
00:19:10,018 --> 00:19:12,771
superiority over
the House of Commons.

276
00:19:12,813 --> 00:19:15,649
A deal only possible
through your actions.

277
00:19:17,318 --> 00:19:21,530
We have something in common.
As the Holmes bear their crime,

278
00:19:21,572 --> 00:19:23,949
so must the Moriarty's
from now on.

279
00:19:23,991 --> 00:19:27,578
As punishment, will you carry
it with you in perpetuity?

280
00:19:28,787 --> 00:19:31,206
[LOUIS]
Yes. I will live.

281
00:19:31,248 --> 00:19:33,083
No, we will live

282
00:19:33,125 --> 00:19:36,753
to pay for the crimes we have
committed against Great Britain.

283
00:19:38,547 --> 00:19:41,049
[ALBERT] I was the one who
asked my brother, William,

284
00:19:41,091 --> 00:19:44,094
to carry out this conspiracy.

285
00:19:44,136 --> 00:19:47,055
The blame for these events
begins and ends with me,

286
00:19:47,097 --> 00:19:49,891
Albert James Moriarty.

287
00:19:49,933 --> 00:19:52,645
I am prepared to
accept the punishment

288
00:19:52,686 --> 00:19:55,481
and to also answer
in William's place.

289
00:19:57,566 --> 00:20:01,612
[MYCROFT] There are several ways
one can assume responsibility.

290
00:20:01,654 --> 00:20:04,573
Imposing such a great
punishment on himself--

291
00:20:04,615 --> 00:20:06,992
that is very much his style.

292
00:20:07,034 --> 00:20:09,953
However...

293
00:20:09,995 --> 00:20:11,372
...he is not alone.

294
00:20:11,413 --> 00:20:13,957
Serving this country to
atone for one's crimes

295
00:20:13,999 --> 00:20:16,335
takes many forms.

296
00:20:16,377 --> 00:20:19,421
Louis, are you sure about this?

297
00:20:19,463 --> 00:20:23,467
[LOUIS] Yes, my convictions
remain unchanged.

298
00:20:23,509 --> 00:20:25,219
[MYCROFT]
If you insist.

299
00:20:26,512 --> 00:20:31,559
[MYCROFT] Louis James Moriarty,
I hereby commit to you

300
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:34,228
the newly-created agency
for intelligence,

301
00:20:34,269 --> 00:20:36,438
which does not officially exist,

302
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:41,443
and answers directly
to Her Majesty, MI Six.

303
00:20:45,364 --> 00:20:46,781
[LOUIS]
I believe with all my heart

304
00:20:46,823 --> 00:20:50,661
William is still
alive, which is why

305
00:20:50,703 --> 00:20:53,330
I must preserve
the legacy he created

306
00:20:53,372 --> 00:20:56,500
and protect this
promising new world.

307
00:20:56,542 --> 00:21:00,754
That is my mission,
as long as I live.

308
00:21:20,566 --> 00:21:22,234
Valkommen.

309
00:21:24,027 --> 00:21:25,279
[HOLMES]
Scotch.

310
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:28,490
Sir, you do know
you're in Switzerland?

311
00:21:29,700 --> 00:21:33,078
[BARTENDER 24A] We drink
kirsch here. Give it a try.

312
00:21:35,748 --> 00:21:37,666
[BARTENDER 24A] I doubt you're
this far into the countryside

313
00:21:37,708 --> 00:21:42,003
on business. Are you out
here chasing after a woman?

314
00:21:42,045 --> 00:21:43,380
Hardly.

315
00:21:43,422 --> 00:21:45,090
I'm looking for a friend.

316
00:21:45,132 --> 00:21:47,092
What sort of friend?

317
00:21:48,260 --> 00:21:50,554
[HOLMES]
Well, let's see.

318
00:21:50,596 --> 00:21:53,474
The kind who would look up
at a spiral staircase

319
00:21:53,515 --> 00:21:56,935
and check for the golden ratio.

320
00:21:56,977 --> 00:22:00,355
Anyone you know? [chuckles]

321
00:22:01,856 --> 00:22:04,318
[WILLIAM chuckles]

322
00:22:04,359 --> 00:22:08,530
[WILLIAM] Catch me if
you can, Mister Holmes.
